course: dictionary
lesson: 14549
title: Petrification: when things turn to stone
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Petrification is a long word, so break it into parts. Petrify means to turn into stone, and the ending -ation turns it into the name of a process. So petrification is the process of turning into stone.
explain: In science, petrification happens to dead plants and animals. «The fallen tree lay under the mud for thousands of years, and slowly its wood underwent petrification.» The clues are thousands of years and slowly, so this change takes a very long time. Minerals seep in and replace the wood, bit by bit, until it is stone.
explain: The word has a second meaning. «The little boy was petrified when the dog barked at him.» Here petrified means so scared that you cannot move. Read the words around it: the barking and the boy's fright show the feeling, not a change into stone. Always check which meaning fits the sentence.
fact: Petrification means the process of turning into stone.
fact: In science, petrification takes a very long time, as minerals slowly replace the material of a dead plant or animal.
fact: Petrified wood, such as in the Petrified Forest in Arizona, is wood that has turned into stone.
fact: «I was petrified» means I was so frightened that I could not move.
fact: In stories, a monster like Medusa can cause petrification, turning people to stone.
exercise: «The wood had changed over millions of years, and now it was solid stone.» What is this change called? | Photosynthesis | *Petrification | Evaporation | Erosion
exercise: «Maya was petrified when the lights went out.» What does petrified mean here? | Turned into stone by a magic spell | Very cold and shivering | Happy and excited | *So scared she could not move
exercise: Which famous monster from stories causes petrification? | Father Christmas | Cinderella's fairy godmother | *Medusa, who turns people to stone | A talking teapot
test: «The Petrified Forest in Arizona is made of wood that has slowly turned to stone.» What does petrified wood mean? | Wood that has been painted bright colours | Wood that has been burned to ash | Wood that is wet and rotten | *Wood that has turned into stone over a long time
test: «Tom stood petrified at the edge of the cliff.» What does petrified mean? | Carved from rock | *So frightened that he could not move | Covered in dust | Very tired and sleepy
exam: Which process turns a dead plant into stone over millions of years? | Erosion | *Petrification | Decay | Germination
